@startuml
' ============================================================================
' METADATA
'   author:       TheRobotDrafts Examples
'   description:  A three-tier system (presentation / application / data)
'                 with assembly connectors, ports, and delegation connectors.
'   usecase:      Teach assembly connectors (ball into socket), ports,
'                 delegation connectors, and downward-only tier dependency.
'   complexity:   medium
'   domain:       layered application architecture
' ============================================================================
title Example Component Diagram - Medium Layered System

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' STYLE: group components into tier packages so the layering reads visually.
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
skinparam componentStyle uml2
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam packageStyle frame

' ===========================================================================
' TIER 1 — PRESENTATION
' Dependencies may only point DOWNWARD (to the tier below), never back up.
' ===========================================================================
package "Presentation Tier" as ptier {
  component "Web UI" as web
  component "Mobile App" as mobile
  ' A PORT exposes a point of interaction on the enclosing component/tier.
  ' Here we model the tier's public-facing port group via the components.
}

' ===========================================================================
' TIER 2 — APPLICATION (business logic)
' ===========================================================================
package "Application Tier" as atier {
  component "API Gateway" as api
  component "Auth Service" as auth
  component "Order Service" as order
  component "Billing Service" as billing
}

' ===========================================================================
' TIER 3 — DATA
' ===========================================================================
package "Data Tier" as dtier {
  database "Orders DB" as ordersDb
  database "Users DB" as usersDb
}

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' ASSEMBLY CONNECTOR: a provided ball plugs directly into a required cup.
' Write it as `[A] -(0- IFoo` style: declare the interface, attach both ends.
' PlantUML renders the ball-and-socket join automatically when one side is
' `-(0-` (provides) and the other is `-(0-` (requires); here we use the
' explicit interface nodes so the contract object is visible.
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

' Presentation -> Application: both clients REQUIRE the gateway contract.
() "REST API" as iRest
api -()- iRest            ' gateway PROVIDES the REST contract
web ..() iRest            ' web client REQUIRES it  (assembly: ball fits socket)
mobile ..() iRest         ' mobile client REQUIRES it

' Internal application wiring: order service needs billing.
() "Charge Card" as iCharge
billing -()- iCharge      ' billing PROVIDES charge capability
order ..() iCharge        ' order REQUIRES it (assembly connector)

' Auth dependency used by both api and order.
() "Verify Token" as iVerify
auth -()- iVerify
api ..() iVerify
order ..() iVerify

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' DELEGATION CONNECTOR: a component forwards a request from an outer port to
' an inner realization. We model delegation by having `api` expose `iRest`
' (above) while internally delegating to `order`. Dotted `..>` from api to
' order shows the internal delegation path.
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
api ..> order : delegates
api ..> auth  : delegates

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' DOWNWARD-ONLY DEPENDENCY: tier 2 uses tier 3 data stores via required
' interfaces. Tier 3 never points back up (no arrows from db -> service).
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
() "Order Repo" as iOrderRepo
ordersDb -()- iOrderRepo
order ..() iOrderRepo

() "User Repo" as iUserRepo
usersDb -()- iUserRepo
auth ..() iUserRepo

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' LEGEND: summarize the three connector families taught here.
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
note bottom of dtier
  **Assembly**    = a provided ball plugs into a required socket (REST, Charge, Repos).
  **Delegation**  = API Gateway forwards outer REST calls to inner Order/Auth.
  **Tier rule**   = arrows always point downward; data tier never points up.
end note

@enduml
